<%- include("partials/header") %>

<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <span class="eyebrow">About RoomSplit</span>
    <h1>Built for renting one home, one room at a time</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="grid grid-2">
  <div class="card">
    <h2>The problem</h2>
    <p>
      Most rental tools assume one owner, one tenant, one lease. Renting by the room means one
      mortgage, several tenants, and shared costs that have to be split fairly.
    </p>
    <h2>The solution</h2>
    <p>
      RoomSplit models the money and tracks the day to day: who lives in which room, who has paid,
      and when each lease ends.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>The spark</h2>
    <p>
      I own a condo in Midtown Atlanta and I'm weighing whether to rent it out by the room.
      I need this exact tool to make that decision, so I'm building it.
    </p>
    <p class="muted small">Uyiosa Nehikhuere &middot; Georgia State University</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-3">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
      <h3>Add your shared costs</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Mortgage, HOA, utilities, internet, and anything else the whole home pays for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
      <h3>Set up rooms and tenants</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Give each room a rent, assign a tenant, and record their lease dates.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
      <h3>Track and compare</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Log payments, spot late rent, and compare renting by the room against renting the whole unit.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section card">
  <h2>Your data stays yours</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="margin: 0;">
    Viewing the dashboard and adding, editing or deleting rooms, tenants, payments and costs all
    require you to be logged in. Each owner only ever sees their own records. You stay logged in
    until you close your browser or click <strong>Log out</strong>.
  </p>
</section>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
